---
/**
 * Accessibility Statement
 *
 * @description
 * 无障碍声明：目标标准（WCAG 2.1 AA）、已采取的措施、已知限制、反馈渠道与响应时限。
 */
import MarketingLayout from '@/layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/config';

const { legal } = siteConfig;
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Accessibility Statement"
  description="How EV Hub approaches accessibility: the standard we work to, the measures already in place, known limitations, and how to report a problem."
>
  <section class="py-section">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <header class="mb-12">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-text">Accessibility Statement</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">Last updated: {legal.lastUpdated}</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
        <p>
          {siteConfig.name} is a research site for importers, analysts and buyers. If the information here cannot be
          read — by a screen reader, by keyboard, at high zoom, or on a slow connection — then it is not doing its job.
          This statement explains the standard we work to and how to tell us when we fall short.
        </p>

        <h2>Standard we aim for</h2>
        <p>
          We target conformance with the <strong>Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA</strong>.
          This is a self-assessed target rather than an audited certification: we review pages as we publish them
          rather than claiming a formal audit we have not commissioned.
        </p>

        <h2>What is in place</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>semantic HTML landmarks and a logical heading order on every page;</li>
          <li>descriptive alternative text for photographs and charts, generated from the same data the page displays;</li>
          <li>keyboard-operable navigation, links and interactive controls, with a visible focus state;</li>
          <li>text and background combinations chosen for contrast, with dark-mode support on system preference;</li>
          <li>responsive layouts that remain usable from narrow phone widths to desktop, and support for browser zoom without loss of content;</li>
          <li>data tables marked up with header cells so screen readers can associate labels with values;</li>
          <li>no autoplaying media, and no content that flashes or animates aggressively.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Known limitations</h2>
        <p>We would rather name these than pretend they do not exist:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Dense data tables.</strong> Landed-cost and comparison tables carry a lot of numbers. They work
            with screen readers, but reading them aloud is verbose; where we can, we also publish the same figures as
            prose in the surrounding text.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Interactive calculators.</strong> The landed-cost calculator needs JavaScript. Without it, the
            underlying method and worked examples remain readable on the methodology pages.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Third-party content.</strong> Embedded or linked material we do not control may not meet the same
            standard.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Ongoing maintenance.</strong> Accessibility is reviewed as part of our publishing and
            maintenance process, and alternative text is generated from the same structured data each page
            displays. If you find a page that is causing you trouble, tell us and it moves to the front of
            the fix queue.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Technical compatibility</h2>
        <p>
          The site is built as static HTML and tested in current versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari on
          desktop and mobile, and with common screen readers (NVDA, JAWS, VoiceOver, TalkBack). Older browsers may
          render it correctly but are not specifically tested.
        </p>

        <h2>How to report a problem</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href={`mailto:${legal.legalEmail}`}>{legal.legalEmail}</a> with the page URL, what you were trying
          to do, the device or assistive technology you were using, and what went wrong. We acknowledge accessibility
          reports within 5 business days, give you a view on whether and when we can fix the issue, and prioritise
          anything that blocks access to information rather than merely inconveniencing it.
        </p>

        <h2>Related policies</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a></li>
          <li><a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a></li>
          <li><a href="/copyright/">Copyright, Trademarks and Takedown Policy</a></li>
          <li><a href="/image-credits/">Image Credits and Copyright</a></li>
          <li><a href="/contact/">Contact</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
